[[eco-serving]]
=== Serving

**STUB**: Specifies how a compiled program is served beyond the command line:
the daemon, the router that fronts several programs, and the transports (HTTP,
TCP and Unix sockets, MCP over stdio). Defines the mapping from one manifest
command to a CLI subcommand, an HTTP endpoint and an MCP tool, including how
argument types become input schemas, how docstrings become descriptions, and
which commands are excluded and why. Specifies remote evaluation of expressions
and the security model: authentication, allow-lists, sandboxing and resource
limits, with the threat each one addresses.

